    "## Reusing a DKS as an initialize state"
   ]
  },
  {
   "attachments": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Sometime it is convenient to seed the simulation with a soliton, for convergence reason or inverse Fourier Transform. To this extend we have implemented the possibility to provide an input that is not zero but instead can be any random vector"
   ]
  },
  {
   "attachments": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In the following cell I am loading the solution from the previous simulation. I saved in a .csv file that is in this folder in which I also saved the detuning at which thte solution has been found. This is needed to be able to stay on the stable branch of the DKS"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv('./DKS_init.csv')\n",
    "df[\"DKS_init\"] = df.DKS_init.apply(lambda val: complex(val.strip('()')))\n",
    "δω = df.det.values[0] * 2*np.pi\n",
    "DKS_init = df.DKS_init.values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "res = dict(\n",
    "        R=23e-6, \n",
    "        Qi=1e6, \n",
    "        Qc=1e6, \n",
    "        γ=3.2, \n",
    "        dispfile=\"./RW1000_H430.csv\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "sim = dict(\n",
    "    Pin=[160e-3], # need to be the same length than fmp\n",
    "    f_pmp=[283e12], # if only one pump f_pmp=[283e12]\n",
    "    φ_pmp=[0], # need to be the same length than fmp\n",
    "    δω=[None], # None defined which pump to sweep\n",
    "    Tscan=0.2e6,\n",
    "    μ_sim=[-220, 220],\n",
    "    δω_end = δω, δω_init = δω, \n",
    "    DKS_init =  DKS_init, \n",
    ")\n",
    "solver = pyLLE.LLEsolver(sim=sim, res=res,debug=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = solver.Analyze(plot=False)\n",
    "solver.Setup(verbose = False)\n",
    "solver.SolveTemporal(bin = \"julia-1.11.1/bin/julia\")\n",
    "solver.RetrieveData()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "attachments": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Note that here I performed a much shorter simulation than in the detuning swept case. It is alright given the convergence of the solution is ok, we did not apply any perturbation to our system and the detuning is fixed. Essentially we are probing how stable the solution is "
   ]
  },
  {
   "attachments": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In the following cell, we will plot the temporal profile of the intracavity field Vs the LLE step and the resoantor angle: "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig = go.Figure()\n",
    "x = np.arange(0, 5000)\n",
    "y = np.linspace(-0.5, 0.5, solver.sol.Acav.shape[0])\n",
    "xsteps = 10\n",
    "ysteps = 2\n",
    "tr = go.Heatmap(x= x[::xsteps], y = y[::ysteps],  z = np.abs(solver.sol.Acav[::ysteps, ::xsteps])**2)\n",
    "fig.add_trace(tr)\n",
    "fig.update_layout(xaxis_title = \"LLE subsampled step\", \n",
    "                 yaxis_title = \"Resonator angle θ (x π)\")\n",
    "                 \n",
    "fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "attachments": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We started with the soliton, and we kept the soliton all along. Great! Seems a bit underwhelming but think that you could potentially apply any perturbative approach through this solver feature (noise, etc...)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "attachments": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Freezing the soliton"
   ]
  },
  {
   "attachments": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In the previous simulation, we can notice that the soliton is actualy drifting with the LLE step, therefore in time. What it actualy means is the normalization of the LLE according to D1 is not the group rotation velocity coordinate of the soliton. It is well know that assymetry in the dispersion can lead to this kind of behavior. \n",
    "However, for many many reason (and I won't go in details here), it is super interesting to freeze the soliton envelope in time. \n",
    "\n",
    "In the solver, this can be simply achieved by implementing a manual D1 value as followed: "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "/zhome/d5/3/214816/viswa/fdtd_py/lib64/python3.9/site-packages/pyLLE/_llesolver.py:549: ComplexWarning:\n",
      "\n",
      "Casting complex values to real discards the imaginary part\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv('./DKS_init.csv')\n",
    "df[\"DKS_init\"] = df.DKS_init.apply(lambda val: complex(val.strip('()')))\n",
    "δω = df.det.values[0] * 2*np.pi\n",
    "DKS_init = df.DKS_init.values\n",
    "\n",
    "res = dict(\n",
    "        R=23e-6, \n",
    "        Qi=1e6, \n",
    "        Qc=1e6, \n",
    "        γ=3.2, \n",
    "        dispfile=\"./RW1000_H430.csv\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "sim = dict(\n",
    "    Pin=[100e-3], # need to be the same length than fmp\n",
    "    f_pmp=[283e12], # if only one pump f_pmp=[283e12]\n",
    "    φ_pmp=[0], # need to be the same length than fmp\n",
    "    δω=[None], # None defined which pump to sweep\n",
    "    Tscan=0.2e6,\n",
    "    μ_sim=[-220, 220],\n",
    "    δω_end = δω, δω_init = δω, \n",
    "    DKS_init =  DKS_init, \n",
    "    D1_manual = 982.2557817183881 * 1e9 * 2*np.pi # linear is 982.2629817183881\n",
    ")\n",
    "solver = pyLLE.LLEsolver(sim=sim, res=res,debug=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = solver.Analyze(plot=False)\n",
    "solver.Setup(verbose = False)"
   ]
  },
